{"content":[{"c":["BILDAD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of three friends who came to comfort Job in his anguish, identified as a Shuhite (",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.11","r":"Job.2.11","rawR":"Job.2.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.11","value":"Job.2.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 2:11"},"). That term suggests that he was a descendant of Shuah, son of Abraham and his second wife Keturah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.25.1-2","r":"Gen.25.1-2","rawR":"Gen.25.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.25.1-2","value":"Gen.25.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 25:1-2"},"). Bildad spoke to Job on three occasions. In his first speech he asserted that God upholds the just and punishes the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Job.8.1-22","r":"Job.8.1-22","rawR":"Job.8.1-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.8.1-22","value":"Job.8.1-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 8"},"). Job must therefore be a hypocrite to say that he is right with God. In his second speech Bildad emphasized the immediate punishment of the wicked in this life (ch ",{"href":"?bref=Job.18.1-21","r":"Job.18.1-21","rawR":"Job.18.1-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.18.1-21","value":"Job.18.1-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"18"},"). Job must therefore be wicked because of his intense suffering. In his third speech Bildad proclaimed the majesty of God and called man a worm by comparison (ch ",{"href":"?bref=Job.25.1-6","r":"Job.25.1-6","rawR":"Job.25.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.25.1-6","value":"Job.25.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"25"},"). He implied that Job was foolish to claim to be righteous before such a holy God."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Job, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bildad","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jb 2:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.2.11","rawQueryValue":"Job.2.11","sourceRefExact":"Job.2.11"},{"anchorText":"Gn 25:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.25.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Gen.25.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Gen.25.1-2"},{"anchorText":"Jb 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.8.1-22","rawQueryValue":"Job.8.1-22","sourceRefExact":"Job.8.1-22"},{"anchorText":"18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.18.1-21","rawQueryValue":"Job.18.1-21","sourceRefExact":"Job.18.1-21"},{"anchorText":"25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.25.1-6","rawQueryValue":"Job.25.1-6","sourceRefExact":"Job.25.1-6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"bf376be1023b4f9963168aeebbf7c7d19a6fd7bf74ce20d08612577005c5308b","sourceItemName":"Bildad","sourceItemOrder":312,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bildad","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bildad","title":"Bildad","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}